	(text "U10 YLPTEC URB2405LD-20WR3: 9-36 V in, 5 V 4 A, 20 W isolated, short-circuit protected, 2\" x 1\" DIP.\nCTRL and Trim open (on, 5.0 V). C34 47 µF (datasheet C1 47-100 µF), C37 / C38 22 µF (C2 / C3 10-22 µF).\nF11 3 A PTC (same part as the relay outputs) + D22 SMF6.0A, then J16: the MES4-Flasher's USB-C\npower-only receptacle, rated 5 V 3 A (3 A on VBUS; GND pins 1.25 A each).\nR48 / R47 10k Rp to 5 V on CC1 / CC2: the monitor sees a Type-C source offering 5 V at 3.0 A.\nR49 1 MΩ || C41 2.2 µF: shell to GND, as on the MES4-Flasher."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 160.02 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "3db6c9e6-851c-5f44-adb9-5b0ab53f9334")
	)
	(text "ARZOPA Z1C label: input 5 / 9 / 12 / 15 / 20 V DC, 3 A max: a USB-PD sink.\nThis port has no PD controller, so it offers 5 V only (15 W max).\nThe sibling Z1RC draws about 9 W (≈ 1.8 A at 5 V), so 5 V / 3 A should\nrun it; check full brightness on the bench. If it needs 9 V or more,\nthe port needs a USB-PD source controller instead.\nVBUS is always on (no cold-socket switch): plug in the monitor, or\nanother sink, only; never a charger or a laptop.\nPower only: the video goes over the monitor's own HDMI / USB-C\nfrom the IPC. Rp is to 5 V: the monitor sinks at most 3 A."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 248.92 114.3 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "29da3cee-ce4f-59d3-9f73-37b5f523c1e0")
	)
